{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LEAF 15f2 — phase 4e, TWO CORRECTIONS TO MY OWN ORACLE.\n\nImplementer delivered 500 lines, visible oracle green on FIRST attempt, 2 hazards FIXED and 24 MARKED\nwith per-test reasons, 'pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit' exit 0 (14,994 collected), lint+typecheck\nclean. It reported census discrepancies rather than reconciling them (1287 files vs my 1261, 869 spawn\nsites vs 866, cwd=REPO_ROOT 23 vs 22; total hazards 26 matched exactly) — exactly what I asked for.\n\nCORRECTION 1 — MY TESTS WERE AT THE WRONG LAYER (implementation was right).\nHeld-out run: 20 passed / 2 failed. Both failures traced to one cause: marker resolution lives in the\nITEM path (item.iter_markers) not in scan_source, which is a marker-blind pure AST scan. That is a\nBETTER design than my contract assumed — pytest's own resolution handles pytestmark, class-level marks\nand inheritance, which an AST scan only approximates. Worse, my blank-marker test was passing for the\nWRONG REASON: it would have passed even with markers entirely unimplemented.\nFixed by testing the real layer: marker admission/rejection now drives unharnessed_subprocess_reason()\nwith fake items exposing iter_markers/path/name/nodeid, and the live-tier check now runs\n'pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit' in a subprocess and asserts exit 0 — the genuine AC2 oracle\ninstead of my scan_source re-derivation. That test needs the opt-out marker itself, which is honest\nand is the documented pattern. 23/23 pass.\n\nCORRECTION 2 — A REAL FALSE NEGATIVE THE IMPLEMENTER SURFACED, AND A GAP IN MY ORACLE.\nIt flagged that my ACCEPT clause ('an env= whose expression contains subprocess_env(, os.environ, or a\n**-spread') is ambiguous, and chose the loose reading. I checked the sites and the loose reading is\nWRONG: tests/unit/test_tracing.py:94 passes env={'PYTHONPATH':'src','PATH':os.environ.get('PATH','')}\nwith NO cwd and NO REBAR_ROOT — the child gets a fresh env without the root, inherits pytest's cwd (the\nrepo root) and falls back to git toplevel = the real checkout. That is the exact defect shape.\nMy oracle MISSED it because my accept-test used a {**os.environ} SPREAD. Added two tests (cherry-picked\nvalue -> hazard; explicit REBAR_ROOT key -> accept), confirmed the first goes RED against the current\nimplementation, and re-dispatched with the tightened rule: a DICT LITERAL accepts only on a **-spread\nof an ambient mapping or an explicit REBAR_ROOT key; an os.environ mention in a VALUE does not accept.\nMoves 6 sites from accept to hazard, to be fixed (preferred) or marked.\n\nLEAF 0880 RESEARCH COMPLETE — headline result is decisive and publishable.\nStep 0: NO OVERLAP with ADR 0109's replay harness (it measures the reviewer's answer stability over\nplan text; it never touches a diff, file count, patchset or caused_by link; confirming grep empty).\nRead (a), n=2,194 merged Gerrit changes 2026-07-01..09-02, 100% sha-matched:\n  FILES-TOUCHED PREDICTS REWORK, LINES DO NOT.\n  Verified-1 rate by files: 1-2 22.7% / 3-5 40.2% / 6-10 46.0% / 11-20 63.5% / >20 58.6%\n  DECISIVE CONTROL: holding non-test LOC at 151-400, widening files moves 41.6 -> 48.2 -> 62.2%;\n  holding files at 3-5, adding LOC is NON-monotonic (34.5 -> 45.8 -> 41.1).\n  Commit fragmentation is a NULL result: 1,616 of 1,793 tickets are single-commit (Gerrit amend-and-\n  repush puts rework in PATCHSETS, not trunk commits).\n  Effect sizes moderate (all rho <= 0.42; worst stratum still 62%, so ~38% false-positive rate) ->\n  supports an ADVISORY rule on file surface, NOT a blocking line-count floor. Matches Prow's\n  non-blocking size/* posture.\nRead (b): 20 of 84 in-window Verified-1 changes substantiated. Classes: drift 9, isolation 4,\nstack/rebase 3, guard-contract 2, attestation 1, plain 1. ZERO were flakes. Cross-session interference\nin 3 (a floor, not a measurement — only detectable where a log says so).\nRead (c): 9 classes C1-C9; highest-return doctor check is C3+C2+C4 as one pre-flight (venv on PATH /\nnot-a-stale-global rebar / provider credential probe / env poisoning) covering 42 of ~90 incidents.\nNine gaps stated precisely, including that Verified-1 root causes are not machine-readable (hence 20\nof 84) and that abandoned changes are excluded so the rates are a LOWER BOUND."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788320905309929001,"uuid":"6d994ef8-bbd6-4a84-ab9a-c306da6b7038"}